<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>There are three common kinds of property claim adjusters: staff adjusters and independent adjusters, who work for the insurer, and public adjusters, who work for the policyholder.</li>
<li>A public claims adjuster is the only one of the three you hire and the only one whose Texas contract must say “WE REPRESENT THE INSURED ONLY.”</li>
<li>Day to day, a public claims adjuster reads the policy, documents the damage, writes the estimate, tracks deadlines, and negotiates the details with the insurer’s adjusters.</li>
<li>Knowing the vocabulary (scope, ACV, recoverable depreciation, supplement, reservation of rights) makes any claim easier to follow, with or without professional help.</li>
